@extends('admin.layouts.app')@section('title','Instagram Session')@section('page_title','Instagram Session')@section('page_subtitle','Pasted once here and used by both this portal and the local worker PC.')@section('content')<div class="row g-3"><div class="col-lg-7"><form class="card" method="post" action="{{ route('admin.instagram.settings.update') }}"><div class="card-body">@csrf @method('PUT')<label class="form-label">Instagram cookie</label><textarea class="form-control" rows="4" name="session_cookie" placeholder="mid=...; ig_did=...; csrftoken=...; sessionid=...">{{ old('session_cookie') }}</textarea><div class="stat-mini mt-1">Leave empty and save to remove the stored session. The saved value is encrypted and never shown back in full.</div><div class="text-end mt-3"><button class="btn btn-primary">Save session</button></div></div></form><div class="card mt-3"><div class="card-body"><h6 class="mb-2">Where to copy it from</h6><ol class="mb-0 ps-3 stat-mini"><li>Log in to Instagram in Chrome with the throwaway account kept for audits, never the company account.</li><li>Open the profile page, press <b>F12</b>, go to the <b>Network</b> tab and click any <code>instagram.com</code> request.</li><li>Under <b>Request Headers</b>, copy the whole <code>Cookie:</code> value and paste it above.</li></ol><div class="stat-mini mt-2">Copying only the <code>sessionid</code> row from the Application tab also works, but Instagram throttles it with HTTP 429 much sooner - the audit then falls back to the profile page, which carries follower counts but no per-post engagement.</div></div></div></div><div class="col-lg-5"><div class="card"><div class="card-body"><h6 class="mb-2">Status</h6>@if(!$session['configured'])<div class="alert alert-warning mb-0">No Instagram session is configured, so profile audits cannot run.</div>@else<table class="table table-sm mb-0"><tr><td>Cookie</td><td class="text-end"><code>{{ $session['preview'] }}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Length</td><td class="text-end">{{ $session['length'] }} characters</td></tr><tr><td>Stored in</td><td class="text-end">{{ $session['stored_in_db'] ? 'Database (this page)' : 'Server .env file' }}</td></tr><tr><td>Whole cookie header</td><td class="text-end">@if($session['whole_header'])<span class="badge bg-success">yes</span>@else<span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">sessionid only</span>@endif</td></tr><tr><td>csrftoken</td><td class="text-end">@if($session['has_csrftoken'])<span class="badge bg-success">present</span>@else<span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">missing</span>@endif</td></tr><tr><td>mid</td><td class="text-end">@if($session['has_mid'])<span class="badge bg-success">present</span>@else<span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">missing</span>@endif</td></tr><tr><td>Last updated</td><td class="text-end">{{ $session['updated_at']?->diffForHumans() ?? '—' }}</td></tr></table>@if(!$session['has_csrftoken'] || !$session['has_mid'])<div class="alert alert-warning mt-3 mb-0">Instagram answers a cookie without <code>csrftoken</code> and <code>mid</code> with HTTP 429, which leaves engagement rate, average likes and posting frequency empty. Paste the whole Cookie header to fix it.</div>@endif @endif</div></div><div class="card mt-3"><div class="card-body"><h6 class="mb-2">Audit route</h6><div class="stat-mini">Mode: <b>{{ $source }}</b>@if($source==='worker') — this server never calls Instagram; audits are queued for the local worker PC, which reads the cookie above through the portal.@elseif($source==='session') — this server calls Instagram itself using the cookie above.@else — anonymous requests, which Instagram answers with a login wall. Set <code>INSTAGRAM_SOURCE=worker</code>.@endif</div>@if($source==='worker' && !$workerReady)<div class="alert alert-danger mt-2 mb-0">INSTAGRAM_WORKER_TOKEN is not set in the server .env, so the worker PC cannot connect.</div>@endif</div></div></div></div>@endsection
